  "diagnosis_text": "Diagnosis: the failed component is the inter-switch link **s3 port 1 \u2194 s1 port 2**.\n\nEvidence:\n- `h1 \u2192 h5` fails completely: **3/3 ICMP lost**.\n- `h1 \u2192 h2`, on the same access switch s3, succeeds: **3/3 received**. This confirms h1 and its s3 host-facing port are working.\n- Topology discovery shows the configured `s1\u2013s3` link is absent from active links.\n- Both ends are administratively/operationally disabled:\n  - `s3-eth1` / **s3 port 1**: `enabled: false`\n  - `s1-eth2` / **s1 port 2**: `enabled: false`\n- s3\u2019s installed forwarding rule for h5\u2019s MAC (`00:00:00:00:00:05`) outputs to **port 1**. The ping traffic is counted on that rule, so packets are being forwarded into the disabled port and black-holed.\n\nAlthough a physical alternate path through s2 exists, the currently installed baseline flow on s3 has not selected it. Thus the immediate reachability failure is caused by the **down s1\u2013s3 link plus stale/non-rerouted forwarding on s3**.\n\nNext step: restore/enable the `s1-eth2`\u2013`s3-eth1` link, or have the controller recompute/reinstall s3\u2019s destination flows to use the live s3\u2013s2 path.",
